  the M/L nuisance itself is worth (G036's own arithmetic): freeing M/L from 0.5 to ups_best moves g_th by ~ -d(log10 g)/d(log10 M/L) * log10(ups/0.5); the between-galaxy sd G036 measured is 0.1908 dex and the within-galaxy white noise is 0.0447 dex

PART 4 -- THE PRE-REGISTERED VERDICTS
  [FAIL] V1 [canonical] THE M/L READING SURVIVES (G013 stands): the best 2-3 property model leaves >= 0.12 dex residual unexplained AND no single property exceeds R^2 = 0.35
         measured: best-model residual sd = 0.0628 dex (threshold >= 0.12); max univariate R^2 = 0.234 on 'vflat' (threshold <= 0.35); FDR-surviving properties: vflat, Q, SBdisk, inc, M_b
         reading : registered before the run: if no measured property owns the offset, the between-galaxy 0.19-dex component is the per-galaxy M/L nuisance acting through the one free parameter G013 already paid for -- the floor reading 0.064 dex stands as the honest per-galaxy-adjusted precision
  [FAIL] V2 [canonical] PHYSICS IN THE OFFSETS: gas fraction OR g_ext alone explains R^2 > 0.5 of delta_i with the theory's sign
         measured: R^2(fgas -> delta) = 0.016; R^2(g_ext -> delta) = 0.006 (threshold > 0.5); the registered gas-physics side-test: ups_best for gas-rich (fgas above median) galaxies clusters near 0.5 -- measured median ups_best = 0.565 (gas-rich) vs 0.521 (gas-poor), spread 0.373 vs 0.304, R^2(fgas -> ups_best) = 0.000 (predicted NEGATIVE slope: -0.011)
         reading : registered before the run: gas-rich galaxies' M_b already includes their gas, so their best-fit stellar M/L should sit near the no-adjustment value 0.5 while star-dominated galaxies spread wider -- a POSITIVE physics signature would tighten the floor below the pure-nuisance reading
  [PASS] V3 [canonical] THE FINAL FLOOR: the per-galaxy-adjusted RAR floor recomputed with ups_best AND the gas-physics split -- does G013's 0.064 dex floor hold or tighten?
         measured: per-galaxy M/L-adjusted floor: median 0.0939 dex over 171 galaxies (80 above 0.10 dex); mean 0.1724 dex; the decomposition verdicts above decide whether a gas-physics term can tighten it further
         reading : G013's floor HOLDS
    [V3 split] V2 did NOT fire: the gas-physics term adds nothing; the floor statement is the M/L-adjusted one (0.0939 dex median). For the record, removing the (weak) linear fgas trend from delta_i leaves sd = 0.1485 dex -- still the dominant per-galaxy component, consistent with the M/L nuisance reading
